{"id": "EUVD-2026-55394", "enisaUuid": "4127a1ea-a43d-3e2c-809f-2294ca111e20", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnet/mlx5: Fix MCIA register buffer overflow on 32 dword reads\n\nThe MCIA register can return up to 32 dwords (128 bytes) when the device\nadvertises the mcia_32dwords capability, but struct\nmlx5_ifc_mcia_reg_bits only defines dword_0..11, leaving room for just\n12 dwords (48 bytes) of data.\n\nmlx5_query_mcia() clamps the read size to mlx5_mcia_max_bytes() and then\nmemcpy()s that many bytes out of the register, potentially reading past\nthe end of the 'out' buffer. On kernels built with FORTIFY_SOURCE this\nis caught as a buffer overflow while reading the module EEPROM via\nethtool:\n\n  detected buffer overflow in memcpy\n  kernel BUG at lib/string_helpers.c:1048!\n  RIP: 0010:fortify_panic+0x13/0x20\n  Call Trace:\n   mlx5_query_mcia.isra.0+0x200/0x210 [mlx5_core]\n   mlx5_query_module_eeprom_by_page+0x4a/0xa0 [mlx5_core]\n   mlx5e_get_module_eeprom_by_page+0xbb/0x120 [mlx5_core]\n   eeprom_prepare_data+0xf3/0x170\n   ethnl_default_doit+0xf1/0x3b0\n\nExtend the mcia_reg layout to 32 dwords.", "datePublished": "2026-08-10T12:02:26", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:43:46", "baseScore": 7.1, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:N/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c8a4acc19dcdc83e1303c29d9535e5c99415a2e3", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5be4eebd5a3a198dab0adcd550e1cadca79bdfed", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/87b39a8c875ca744b7de69af0a8ef8874cffccf1", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/88b2a16ddac3357e3f1d528e758b51e2c945d546", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/11c057d23465c7a5817a7284c896d19d54c0b616"], "aliases": ["GHSA-7555-mcj4-25r2", "CVE-2026-68293"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.14, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0333f4fb-be1b-33fb-bc65-caf316d06102", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.1.6"}, {"id": "058e61a2-ed6c-31fa-8ce8-f8fe565ec30d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "271907ee2f29cd1078fd219f0778fd824fb1971c <c8a4acc19dcdc83e1303c29d9535e5c99415a2e3"}, {"id": "168caf33-64f0-384e-b003-e895fbc3c976", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "271907ee2f29cd1078fd219f0778fd824fb1971c <87b39a8c875ca744b7de69af0a8ef8874cffccf1"}, {"id": "23166290-025f-3a4f-b850-6d74616e10fa", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "271907ee2f29cd1078fd219f0778fd824fb1971c <11c057d23465c7a5817a7284c896d19d54c0b616"}, {"id": "2a816217-7813-3e8f-824c-62db7fa8a589", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.101"}, {"id": "3802a5b3-dd21-3768-92bb-cc8e1c81cb05", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "271907ee2f29cd1078fd219f0778fd824fb1971c <5be4eebd5a3a198dab0adcd550e1cadca79bdfed"}, {"id": "963b5716-c137-302e-ad98-a0201af002c9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.42"}, {"id": "b00c23de-121d-36bb-a223-9decaa9d9d3a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2"}, {"id": "b373ff97-e7c9-3330-9812-0438d914164c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "271907ee2f29cd1078fd219f0778fd824fb1971c <88b2a16ddac3357e3f1d528e758b51e2c945d546"}, {"id": "ba15ce88-26c1-36f9-9caa-09e505c95902", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.18"}, {"id": "d0ae5d14-fc86-3f98-b629-2f42b3ce3dce", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "e49ae9c9-b5f5-3b50-9594-d6a88f098266", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "43006eb3-fa0f-3438-bdc9-82cd86751267", "vendor": {"na